{
  "case_id": "2021-20-637",
  "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Jeffrey L. Fisher)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Fisher: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: A defendant cannot lose his right under the Confrontation Clause to exclude testimonial hearsay simply by making a legitimate defense based on admissible evidence, and that is true even if the hearsay the prosecution would like to introduce would supposedly contradict that defense. To the contrary, history and experience tell us that is when the clause's guarantee of cross-examination is at its most urgent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Hemphill versus New York. Mr. Fisher."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: A couple of quick questions, Mr. Fisher."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Fisher, under what theory would Reid be constitutional? I thought Reid basically said you can open the door to testimonial hearsay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can I take you back to Justice Thomas's first question about what you did and did not raise in the court of appeals?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the state has openly admitted in its brief that it has no historical support for the rule that it's arguing for today."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Don't you think it's a bit odd that the court of appeals disposed of this on an abuse-of-discretion standard, that if it had been -- that if it thought it had a constitutional issue before it, it would not have disposed of it on that standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Why not? With the statement about the 9-millimeter casing found, where else would it have come from?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mignola",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now you have recognized, I think, that the Petitioner is asking for a broad and sweeping rule. He's essentially claiming that a defendant can never open the door to the admission of evidence that would otherwise be barred by the Confrontation Clause. It doesn't matter if a defendant has misled the jury, and, really, if his approach is taken to its extreme, even the traditional rule of completeness would fall."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Fisher gave some examples in the record as to why he raised -- Petitioner raised the Confrontation Clause issue below. Would you address those specifics that he raised?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So if -- isn't there two ways to prevent the jury from being misleaded -- misled? The first is simply to -- to keep out what the defense is proffering."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But weren't there --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Jeffrey L. Fisher)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. I'd like to make one point on preservation and then two points on the merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the prosecution's evidence would be contrary to the defense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7fad066abf1d30f6549a4c09421aa9864ea592b02da36a981679d4e7049f0e3a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7fad066abf1d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
